# Machine-specific settings for this checkout.
#
# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in only what you need. Every line is
# optional: the path resolvers discover the Google Drive mount on their own, so
# a Mac signed in to the research Drive usually needs no .env for data paths.
# Values already set in your shell win over this file.
#
# Loaded automatically by research/ftir_hips_chem/scripts/pls_transfer.py (so
# every data_paths resolver), scripts/common/paths.py, the `aeth` CLI and the
# Zoer data-space recipes (aethmodular_cli/env.py). Not by config.py: its hash
# is pinned by the frozen source audits. `uv run aeth doctor` shows what
# resolved. `~` is expanded.

# --- Google Drive research archive -----------------------------------------
# The "My Drive" folder. Default: ~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-*/My Drive
# AETHMODULAR_DRIVE_ROOT=~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-you@example.com/My Drive

# The raw-data root ("Davis Data"). Default: probed under the Drive root.
# AETHMODULAR_MAIA_DATA_ROOT=

# Individual datasets, only when one lives outside the layout above
# (e.g. a local copy of a file Drive will not materialize).
# AETHMODULAR_FTIR_SPECTRA_DIR=
# AETHMODULAR_FTIR_LOCAL_DB=

# Without Drive for Desktop (a cloud container, CI): `uv run aeth drive mirror`
# copies the shared "Davis Data" folder down and prints the lines above to set.
# The folder id is the last part of the share link; keep it here, never in git.
# AETHMODULAR_DRIVE_ROOT must then hold
# University/Research/Grad/Data/Davis Data (`--link-root` makes that symlink),
# because pls_transfer.FTIRTransferPaths reads only the Drive root.
# See docs/gallery-data-pipeline.md.
# DAVIS_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID=
# AETHMODULAR_ETAD_DIR=
# AETHMODULAR_AETHALOMETRY_DIR=
# AETHMODULAR_WEATHER_DIR=
# AETHMODULAR_IMPROVE_DIR=
# AETHMODULAR_AERONET_DIR=
# AETHMODULAR_PORTAL_DIR=
# AETHMODULAR_DAVIS_DIR=
# The extracted python_pmf package (Addis Python PMF, Oct 2026) for gallery/data/export_python_pmf.py:
# AETHMODULAR_PYTHON_PMF_DIR=

# Raw HIPS internals export from get_hips_internals.ps1. Default:
# ~/Downloads/hips/spartan_hips_raw_all.csv if present, else the copy under
# "Davis Data/DAVIS/SPARTAN HIPS pulls".
# AETHMODULAR_HIPS_RAW_CSV=

# In-repo processed data. Default: research/ftir_hips_chem
# config.py reads this at import but does not load .env, so from .env it only
# takes effect when data_paths/pls_transfer are imported first (or export it).
# AETHMODULAR_DATA_ROOT=

# --- Services ----------------------------------------------------------------
# SQL export sessions on the institution-connected Windows machine only.
# Set in that Windows session; the runbook does not print its value.
# Include Database=Networks_1_0, Integrated Security=SSPI, Connect Timeout=60.
# AETHMODULAR_AQRC_CONNECTION_STRING=

# NASA Earthdata Login user token, for `aeth maia pull` (ASDC MAIA granules).
# Make one at https://urs.earthdata.nasa.gov/profile -> Generate Token. The
# MAIA catalogue (`aeth maia catalog`) needs no login.
# EARTHDATA_TOKEN=

# Zoer server root used by research/ftir_hips_chem/workflows/data_space_recipes.
# Required for those recipes; nothing else reads it.
# ZOER_URL=https://zoer.example.org

# Codex presentations runtime used by the .mjs deck builders under
# research/ftir_hips_chem/workflows (codex_presentations_runtime.mjs). Those
# are Node scripts and read this file themselves.
# Default: $CODEX_HOME (else ~/.codex)/plugins/cache/openai-primary-runtime/
#          presentations/26.909.12148/skills/presentations
# AETHMODULAR_CODEX_PRESENTATIONS_DIR=
# Default: ~/.cache/codex-runtimes/codex-primary-runtime/dependencies/python/bin/python3
# AETHMODULAR_CODEX_PYTHON=

# Local OpenResearch instance and its file store.
# OPENRESEARCH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4791
# OPENRESEARCH_FILES_DIR=~/.local/share/openresearch/files

# Unpacked native network CSV bundles for the gallery site/spectrum exporter.
# AETHMODULAR_SPARTAN_FTIR_BUNDLE=
# AETHMODULAR_SPARTAN_HIPS_BUNDLE=
